## Why This Is Asked
This probes low-level I/O pacing, NUMA locality, and concurrency under contention; it tests both design and practical skeleton implementation.

## Key Concepts
- I/O throttling and quotas
- Token bucket algorithm
- NUMA-aware data structures and per-CPU queues
- Atomic CAS and lock-free coordination
- Wakeups, timers, and tail-latency testing

## Code Example
```c
// Pseudo-C implementation sketch
typedef struct io_quota {
  atomic_long tokens;
  long refill_rate; // tokens/ms
  wait_queue_t *wait;
} io_quota_t;

bool submit_io(io_task_t *t, size_t bytes) {
  long old = atomic_fetch_sub(&t->quota->tokens, bytes);
  if (old >= (long)bytes) return true; // enough tokens
  atomic_fetch_add(&t->quota->tokens, bytes); // revert
  enqueue_wait(t->quota->wait, t);
  return false;
}
```

